00:52:16.280 --> 00:52:21.180
Speaking of hairstyles, Jenna, I wrote about my hair in my journal for this episode.
说到发型，珍娜，我在这一集的日记里写到了我的头发。

1415
00:52:21.660 --> 00:52:23.800
I, I, I'm juSt.
我，我，我只是。

1416
00:52:24.920 --> 00:52:25.800
What?
什么？

1417
00:52:26.340 --> 00:52:36.460
Listen, lady, if you had had to wear a tight bun with a gazillion bobby pins poking you for like every day, you would definitely, if you're, something changed,
听着，女士，如果你每天都得梳紧紧的发髻，还得插上无数根发夹扎得你生疼，那你肯定，如果你是，有什么改变的话，

1418
00:52:36.600 --> 00:52:37.500
you might write about it.
你可能也会写下来。

1419
00:52:37.560 --> 00:52:38.160
And I did.
而我确实写了。

1420
00:52:38.160 --> 00:52:39.600
So here we go.
所以我们开始吧。

1421
00:52:39.800 --> 00:52:41.040
This is what I said.
我是这么写的。

1422
00:52:41.200 --> 00:52:44.740
On a small note, I, for once, like my hair in this episode.
顺便提一下，我破天荒地喜欢这一集里自己的发型。

1423
00:52:45.840 --> 00:52:49.560
Angela always wears the crazy braids, the buns, the ponytails.
安吉拉总是梳着夸张的辫子、发髻和马尾辫。

1424
00:52:49.780 --> 00:52:53.040
But I guess being in a relationship has made her step it up a little.
但我想谈恋爱让她稍微提升了一下形象。

1425
00:52:53.260 --> 00:52:53.700
Ooh.
噢。

1426
00:52:54.080 --> 00:52:54.400
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1427
00:52:54.400 --> 00:52:55.380
I like that backstory.
我喜欢这个背景故事。

1428
00:52:55.640 --> 00:52:55.880
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1429
00:52:55.960 --> 00:52:57.460
I got to wear my hair down.
我终于可以披散着头发了。

1430
00:52:57.620 --> 00:52:58.020
You did.
你确实披着。

1431
00:52:58.200 --> 00:52:59.200
And I was really excited.
我当时真的很兴奋。

1432
00:52:59.420 --> 00:53:00.920
It had a little bit of a boof on.
头发还有点蓬松感。

1433
00:53:00.920 --> 00:53:04.220
I actually thought your hair looked really pretty in this episode.
我其实觉得你这一集里的发型看起来真的很漂亮。

1434
00:53:04.340 --> 00:53:04.720
Oh, thank you.
噢，谢谢。

1435
00:53:04.720 --> 00:53:10.840
I have to say, I'm now, I'm, I was teasing you about writing your journal about it, but I mean, yeah.
我得说，我现在，我，我刚才是在拿你写日记的事开玩笑，但我是说，确实。

1436
00:53:11.140 --> 00:53:12.700
Well, it was journal worthy.
嗯，这确实值得写进日记里。

1437
00:53:13.000 --> 00:53:13.420
Thank you.
谢谢。

1438
00:53:13.420 --> 00:53:17.020
It was the first episode that I didn't have my hair up in any way.
这是我第一次没有把头发盘起来的一集。

1439
00:53:17.120 --> 00:53:17.340
No.
没错。

1440
00:53:17.500 --> 00:53:18.400
So I wrote about it.
所以我写了下来。

1441
00:53:18.680 --> 00:53:18.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1442
00:53:19.060 --> 00:53:19.860
It's very nice.
非常好看。

1443
00:53:20.360 --> 00:53:26.300
So now at 12 minutes, 20 seconds, we meet Billy Merchant, who is played by Marcus York, as we discussed.
现在到了12分20秒，我们见到了比利·莫钱特，正如我们讨论过的，由马库斯·约克饰演。

1444
00:53:26.480 --> 00:53:27.980
And he is the property manager.
他是物业经理。

1445
00:53:28.360 --> 00:53:28.760
Yes.
是的。

1446
00:53:29.000 --> 00:53:31.520
And Jenna, he's here to just tell us information, right?
珍娜，他来这里只是为了通知我们一些信息，对吧？

1447
00:53:31.620 --> 00:53:32.540
About the parking lot.
关于停车场的事。

1448
00:53:32.820 --> 00:53:36.320
Tell us not to block the loading dock, even if we have our hazards on.
告诉我们不要堵住装卸区，即使我们开了危险报警闪光灯也不行。

1449
00:53:36.580 --> 00:53:39.480
He just wants to tell us some stuff about the building.
他只是想告诉我们一些关于大楼的事情。

1450
00:53:39.720 --> 00:53:39.960
Right.
没错。

1451
00:53:40.120 --> 00:53:41.160
Some of the building rules.
关于一些建筑规则。

1452
00:53:41.160 --> 00:53:43.460
And you said Michael sees this as an opportunity.
你说迈克尔把这看作是一个机会。

1453
00:53:43.780 --> 00:53:44.120
Yes.
是的。

1454
00:53:44.340 --> 00:53:51.100
Because Billy is in a wheelchair, Michael has decided that he's pretty sure Billy is going
因为比利坐着轮椅，迈克尔认定比利肯定会

1455
00:53:51.100 --> 00:53:57.240
to lecture us about the proper way to treat disabled people and back up the fact that
教导我们该如何正确对待残疾人，并以此来证明

1456
00:53:57.240 --> 00:53:58.780
Michael has been so wronged.
迈克尔受了多大的委屈。

1457
00:53:58.800 --> 00:54:00.520
Oh, Michael's been so wronged, right?
哦，迈克尔受了天大的委屈，对吧？

1458
00:54:00.660 --> 00:54:00.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1459
00:54:01.200 --> 00:54:04.980
So Marcus said that they really stuck to the script, him and Steve, for this scene.
马库斯说他和史蒂夫在这一幕里确实是照着剧本演的。

1460
00:54:05.060 --> 00:54:05.260
Okay.
好的。

1461
00:54:05.320 --> 00:54:07.360
But then Steve threw an improv at him.
但后来史蒂夫对他即兴发挥了一下。

1462
00:54:07.480 --> 00:54:08.580
I think I know what it is.
我想我知道是什么了。

1463
00:54:08.620 --> 00:54:08.920
Yes.
没错。

1464
00:54:08.920 --> 00:54:13.520
So he said that Steve said, well, you know, we have a lot in common.
他说史蒂夫当时说，嗯，你知道，我们有很多共同点。

1465
00:54:13.880 --> 00:54:16.960
And then he says, I'm going to stop you right there and leave.
然后他说，我要打断你一下，我要走了。

1466
00:54:17.100 --> 00:54:18.100
That's all scripted.
那都是剧本里的。

1467
00:54:18.180 --> 00:54:18.320
Yeah.
是啊。

1468
00:54:18.800 --> 00:54:21.180
But then Steve improvised, who, me?
但史蒂夫即兴加了一句：谁，我吗？

1469
00:54:21.460 --> 00:54:24.220
And Billy goes, no, me, right now.
然后比利说：不，是我，就现在。

1470
00:54:24.420 --> 00:54:26.080
He, like, improvised that right back.
他就像是即兴回击了过去。

1471
00:54:26.240 --> 00:54:28.300
And I was like, that was great, Marcus.
当时我就觉得，马库斯，那太棒了。

1472
00:54:28.300 --> 00:54:29.440
That was so good.
那真是太好了。

1473
00:54:29.820 --> 00:54:32.480
Marcus said that he wasn't, like, ready for that improv.
马库斯说他当时没准备好应对那种即兴发挥。

1474
00:54:32.660 --> 00:54:33.500
Like, he wasn't sure.
他不太确定。

1475
00:54:33.500 --> 00:54:36.800
He said, you know, when you guest star on a show, you don't know.
他说，你知道，当你去客串一部剧时，你心里没底。

1476
00:54:36.860 --> 00:54:38.260
Did they stick to the script?
他们是照着剧本演的吗？

1477
00:54:38.480 --> 00:54:38.580
Yeah.
是的。

1478
00:54:38.640 --> 00:54:41.440
Like, he had heard that we had a lot of improv background and things like that.
他听说过我们有很强的即兴表演背景之类的。

1479
00:54:41.460 --> 00:54:44.240
But he said that Steve just kind of threw that.
但他没想到史蒂夫会突然来那么一下。

1480
00:54:44.340 --> 00:54:45.480
And then he just reacted.
然后他就顺势反应了。

1481
00:54:45.480 --> 00:54:47.860
And that's, like, something he remembers as being really fun.
他说那段经历让他觉得特别有趣。

1482
00:54:48.040 --> 00:54:50.920
Well, when Steve says that line, you know what?
好吧，当史蒂夫说那句台词时，你知道吗？

1483
00:54:50.920 --> 00:54:53.980
We aren't that different when I clamp my foot on the George Foreman grill.
当我把脚夹在乔治·福尔曼烤架上时，我们也没什么不同。

1484
00:54:54.220 --> 00:54:58.620
You see Mindy put her hand up to her mouth.
你可以看到明迪把手捂到了嘴上。

1485
00:54:59.120 --> 00:55:03.660
And then you see me full-on laugh and turn to Rain.
然后你看到我彻底笑场了，还转头看向雷恩。

